#!/bin/sh
# Change Isolation (engineering/change-isolation), as local feedback before a push: Core travels
# alone, .github travels alone. The rules live only in the checker; this hook supplies the change set
# the same way the GitHub workflow does. GitHub's check stays the authority.
#
# Enable once per clone: git config core.hooksPath .githooks
# Target: the PR base this branch is meant for. Name it once per branch with
#   git config branch.<branch>.kaalTarget origin/kaal/genesis   (or origin/main)
# Unnamed, the target is the remote's default branch only while the work shares no history with a
# kaal/* lineage beyond it; otherwise the push is not verified until the target is named. Judged
# against your last fetch of the target; skip once with git push --no-verify.
remote=${1:-origin}
default=$(git symbolic-ref --quiet --short "refs/remotes/$remote/HEAD" 2>/dev/null || echo "$remote/main")
tmp=$(mktemp -d) || exit 1
trap 'rm -rf "$tmp"' EXIT
status=0
while read -r local_ref head remote_ref remote_head; do
  case $head in *[!0]*) ;; *) continue ;; esac # a deleted ref carries no change
  if git merge-base --is-ancestor "$head" "$default" 2>/dev/null; then
    continue # synchronization: already admitted on the default branch
  fi
  branch=${local_ref#refs/heads/}
  target=
  [ "$branch" != "$local_ref" ] && target=$(git config "branch.$branch.kaalTarget")
  if [ -z "$target" ]; then
    lineages=$(git for-each-ref --format='%(refname:short)' "refs/remotes/$remote/kaal/" | while read -r l; do
      base=$(git merge-base "$head" "$l") && ! git merge-base --is-ancestor "$base" "$default" && echo "$l"
    done)
    if [ -n "$lineages" ]; then
      echo "Change Isolation: not verified: $local_ref shares history with" $lineages "beyond $default." >&2
      if [ "$branch" != "$local_ref" ]; then
        echo "  Name its PR target: git config branch.$branch.kaalTarget <ref>" >&2
      else
        echo "  Push it from a branch and name that branch's PR target." >&2
      fi
      status=1
      continue
    fi
    target=$default
  fi
  if ! git show "$target:engineering/change-isolation/check.mjs" >"$tmp/check.mjs" 2>/dev/null; then
    echo "Change Isolation: not verified: $target does not hold engineering/change-isolation/check.mjs" >&2
    status=1
    continue
  fi
  git diff --no-ext-diff --no-relative --no-renames --name-only -z --end-of-options "$target...$head" \
    >"$tmp/paths" && node "$tmp/check.mjs" <"$tmp/paths" >&2 || {
    echo "Change Isolation: $local_ref does not conform against $target" >&2
    status=1
  }
done
exit $status
